  "description": "Canonical cross-binding byte/value contract (bead esd-heg.6) for the DUO primal-cell geometry FAQ at icosahedral level 0. Every conforming binding (Julia/Rust/Python) MUST reproduce these exact Float64 values for cell area (spherical excess, L'Huilier, m^2), cell-center cartesian centroid (cart_x/y/z, m), and geographic lon/lat (rad) from the fixed base icosahedron, computed by the value-invention geometry FAQ in primal_geometry.esm. Values are shortest round-trippable decimals; the contract is bitwise Float64 identity (parse then compare bit patterns), not raw decimal-string identity. Pinned by test/test_duo_primal_geometry_faq.jl, which checks both the FAQ (ESS eval_coeff) and the imperative build_duo_grid reproduce them to 0 ULP.",
